<speak>
<s>This is your briefing for <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">13042026</say-as>.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="95%">
<s>The United States has blockaded all Iranian ports after twenty-one hours of ceasefire talks in Islamabad collapsed over uranium enrichment.</s> <s>US Central Command confirmed the order applies to vessels of every nation transiting the Strait of Hormuz — the waterway that carries a fifth of the world's energy — and Brent crude has crossed one hundred dollars a barrel.</s> <s>Two American carrier groups now face Iranian positions in the strait, and Tehran says the waterway remains under its control.</s>
</prosody>
<p>
<s>In politics.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Britain and France are building a coalition against the blockade — because it traps allied shipping from the Philippines to Japan, not just Iranian cargo.</s> <s>London is sending minesweepers into a waterway it refuses to help blockade, a direct break with Washington not seen since the Iraq war.</s> <s>Trump says NATO will help clear the strait, but NATO's two largest European navies are now working to keep it open.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Viktor Orbán's sixteen-year grip on Hungary ended Sunday.</s> <s>The centre-right Tisza party took fifty-two percent to Fidesz's thirty-nine — not a leftward shift, but a protest vote against a leader who'd aligned with both Trump and Putin while the economy stagnated.</s> <s>Peter Magyar now governs, but winning an election and dismantling sixteen years of captured institutions are very different tasks.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Nigerian military jets struck a village market in Yobe State on Saturday, killing around two hundred people.</s> <s>The air force claimed a Boko Haram target, but this is Nigeria's third mass civilian bombing since twenty-seventeen — a refugee camp, a fishing village, and now a market.</s> <s>Amnesty International is calling for an independent investigation, though past calls have produced no accountability.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Five Israeli divisions have encircled Bint Jbeil in southern Lebanon, sealing every access route, but Hezbollah's fighters have held off entry.</s> <s>The offensive appears timed to undermine ceasefire talks — and in Gaza, Hamas rejected a UN eight-month disarmament timeline, saying Israel hasn't met its own Phase Two withdrawal commitments.</s> <s>Two separate negotiation tracks, in Islamabad and at the UN, are now stalled at the same time.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Trump called Pope Leo the Fourteenth "weak on crime" after the pontiff urged one point four billion Catholics to pressure their lawmakers against the Iran war.</s> <s>Leo had called Trump's threat to destroy Iranian civilization "truly unacceptable" — the sharpest Vatican rebuke of a sitting American president in modern memory.</s> <s>Catholic legislators aligned with the White House now face direct pressure from Rome, and the Vatican hasn't responded.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>On the economy.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Pakistan's liquefied natural gas imports have collapsed since Hormuz closed, and the government is now choosing between seven million gas consumers and thirty million electricity users — it can't supply both.</s> <s>Saudi Arabia and Qatar stepped in with five billion dollars, but the money comes from the very states hosting the war Pakistan was trying to mediate.</s> <s>What Riyadh wants in return hasn't been stated.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Spain's prime minister told Xi Jinping in Beijing that the EU-China trade imbalance is unsustainable — while simultaneously deepening ties as a hedge against Washington.</s> <s>Spain's deficit with China grew eighteen percent last year, and Trump threatened Madrid's trade after it denied bases for strikes on Iran.</s> <s>Europe is criticizing China's surplus with one hand and clinging to it with the other.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Poland signed three point eight billion dollars in Korean missile contracts last December — the largest Asian arms purchase by any NATO member in Europe.</s> <s>Warsaw turned east because American reliability has declined and European defence factories simply can't scale fast enough.</s> <s>In sha'Allah the post-American defence order now taking shape will hold — but for now, it's being built one arms deal at a time.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Seventeen point eight million South Africans are now food insecure, up from fourteen million in twenty-nineteen.</s> <s>Thirty percent unemployment and the Hormuz fuel price shock are threading through supply chains, and twenty-nine percent of children under five are already stunted.</s> <s>The price shock hasn't yet reached supermarket shelves — when it does, those numbers will climb.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Sweden's coast guard boarded a Panama-flagged ship dumping coal waste in the Baltic while hauling Russian cargo.</s> <s>Flag-of-convenience registries let shipowners dodge the environmental laws of every country their cargo touches — a loophole the Baltic's shadow fleet has exploited for years.</s> <s>The master admitted guilt and paid a deposit, but whether Swedish prosecutors pursue criminal charges remains open.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In science.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>The <sub alias="Intergovernmental Panel on Climate Change">IPCC</sub> is running out of money — the body whose reports are the only evidence base Pacific Island nations have to unlock adaptation funds at UN climate talks.</s> <s>Australia, the regional power positioned to push institutional reform, hasn't acted.</s> <s>If the <sub alias="I P C C">IPCC</sub> can't fund its next assessment cycle, the most climate-vulnerable nations on Earth lose their strongest scientific advocate.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>India launched its first indigenous quantum computers in Amaravati — machines running at near-absolute-zero without a single IBM or Google component.</s> <s>Amaravati One-S and One-Q give India a hardware certification capability it previously lacked, and the facility opens tomorrow.</s> <s>Quantum startups that've been renting Western cloud hardware now have a domestic alternative.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In technology.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>A three point six billion parameter AI model costing eleven cents per million tokens has reproduced a zero-day exploit that only frontier security tools were supposed to find.</s> <s>Security teams built their threat models around the assumption that only the largest, most expensive models could discover software vulnerabilities — that assumption is now broken.</s> <s>The moat, it turns out, isn't the model... it's the pipeline around it.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Someone threw a Molotov cocktail at Sam Altman's home at three forty-five in the morning.</s> <s>An essay circulating the same week argues AI displacement is following the Luddite pattern — economic anxiety channelling into attacks on visible corporate targets, with no political answer in sight.</s> <s>Altman wrote that he'd underestimated how displacement anxiety converts to violence, and so far no one's been charged.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Researchers have built a wound dressing that cools burns without electricity — a silica layer reflects ninety-two percent of sunlight while a drug layer underneath delivers antibiotics.</s> <s>Simulations showed peak cooling of a hundred and sixty-eight watts per square metre in Cairo, precisely where grid power is least reliable.</s> <s>A bandage engineered to work best where infrastructure doesn't — that's the kind of design the world actually needs.</s>
</p>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="90%">
<s>That's your briefing.</s>
</prosody>
</speak>